{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531774-a-slasher-mimicking-the-judges","id":1531774,"title":"A Slasher mimicking The Judges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-01T03:34:47-08:00","id":1531774,"title":"A Slasher mimicking The Judges","content":"While thinking up potential Slasher ideas to use I thought up an interesting one.<br /> <br /> Sir John Quincy Harrow-Smith, a well respected and decorated Egyptologist who has a secret fascination for Irem , The Nameless Empire, and Duat. During the course of these studies he somehow becomes obsessed with The Judges and begins picking off &quot;sinners&quot; in ways he envisions each Judge killing them.<br /> <br /> At first, these victims are genuinely bad people, but over time Sir John begins targeting those whose only crime was something minor that would still annoy a judge.<br /> <br /> He would be an Avenger undertaking of course.<br /> <br /> Could this idea work and do you guys have any ideas on how to make it more interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T04:45:06-08:00","id":1531777,"title":"","content":"My first question is &quot;why a slasher&quot;? That's going to be less than a speed bump for a Mummy, and a cult or singular cultist is more appropriate to a Mummy game.<br /> <br /> Second, I would ask how he learned of Irem and the Judges. It takes more than digging around in the Sahara to learn of them, much less come to the accurate conclusion that they truly exist. Maybe his family has been in service to one or more mummies for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> I don't think &quot;mimicking the Judges&quot; is all that compelling a motivation for a slasher, not all the judges are crazed psychopaths. I think I would tie him to either one particular judge, he's killing because he is obsessed and wants attention on a personal level. Maybe he thinks the judge is his father, either spiritually or literally.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, maybe he wants to re-enact the Rite of Return and needs all the Judges' attention and blessing to do it. Human sacrifice was a big part of that rite.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":".  Clarifying a point 03-01-2024, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T17:43:30-08:00","id":1531936,"title":"","content":"If you're going to have a slasher acting like that, wouldn't it be better for him to be a Beast? This would make him stronger, give him more resources and it would be simple to relate this fanaticism to the hunger of the beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T18:56:45-08:00","id":1531940,"title":"","content":"I'm going to engage in the actual premise of the thread, <br /> Yes a Slasher can work.<br /> <br /> So a Slasher trying to enforce what they believe is the Will of the Judges of Duat.<br /> Interesting idea, need to know who they are meant to be an antagonist for...<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27618_2.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27618\" data-vbnamecard=\"27618\">ShadowcatX</a> isn't wrong in that one of the Arisen could basically just crush him under heel. Wasn't inaccurate about learning about Irem either.<br /> <br /> Urgo, someone (an Arisen, an Immortal, a sorcerer or the like) showed Sir John, enough that turned a storied and respected academic into a fanatical believer. Taught him of the Judges and their laws, possibly even how to recognize their servants (Mummies &amp; their cults). Probably not out of the kindness of their heart either. Regardless with a better framework, Harrow-Smith may have figured out sorcery on his own. While the killings might not have been the plan, they may have their use. <br /> So Sir John Quincy Harrow-Smith has a backer and may have become a sorcerer in addition to a Slasher. Someone had a plan for him and now he is armed with supernatural abilities.<br /> <br /> That is plenty for a Hunter game and has enough meat for a Mummy game. It gives steps forward after he has been delt with.<br /> <br /> Haven't worked out what the twist is, beyond the obvious &quot;the secret backer is ...&quot;. Maybe Sir John is trying to earn a Crown, (ie. become a benbenet).<br /> <br /> Still a good session or two, depending on how long the players take to solve the investigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T19:25:09-08:00","id":1531942,"title":"","content":"How about making them a Legend ? They mimic a tale that illustrates the Judge's field of duty, with the slasher acting as the character that delivers their judgement. Perhaps they believe that it brings their will closer to the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T12:35:09-08:00","id":1531974,"title":"","content":"Yeah, he was meant for Hunter, not Mummy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T14:50:55-08:00","id":1531980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531774-a-slasher-mimicking-the-judges?p=1531940#post1531940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to engage in the actual premise of the thread,<br /> Yes a Slasher can work.<br /> <br /> So a Slasher trying to enforce what they believe is the Will of the Judges of Duat.<br /> Interesting idea, need to know who they are meant to be an antagonist for...<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27618_2.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27618\" data-vbnamecard=\"27618\">ShadowcatX</a> isn't wrong in that one of the Arisen could basically just crush him under heel. Wasn't inaccurate about learning about Irem either.<br /> <br /> Urgo, someone (an Arisen, an Immortal, a sorcerer or the like) showed Sir John, enough that turned a storied and respected academic into a fanatical believer. Taught him of the Judges and their laws, possibly even how to recognize their servants (Mummies &amp; their cults). Probably not out of the kindness of their heart either. Regardless with a better framework, Harrow-Smith may have figured out sorcery on his own. While the killings might not have been the plan, they may have their use.<br /> So Sir John Quincy Harrow-Smith has a backer and may have become a sorcerer in addition to a Slasher. Someone had a plan for him and now he is armed with supernatural abilities.<br /> <br /> That is plenty for a Hunter game and has enough meat for a Mummy game. It gives steps forward after he has been delt with.<br /> <br /> Haven't worked out what the twist is, beyond the obvious &quot;the secret backer is ...&quot;. Maybe Sir John is trying to earn a Crown, (ie. become a benbenet).<br /> <br /> Still a good session or two, depending on how long the players take to solve the investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the twist is that the slasher and the murders aren't the point, maybe the characters triumphing over the slasher is the point. Maybe the backer needs a symbolic win over something representing the judges for a spell? <br /> <br /> And I do think as a Hunter villain this works much better than a Mummy villain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}